  "description": "The deployment consists of two Docker services, **web** and **db**, each configured with a full set of runtime options.\n\nThe **web** service is built from the current directory (`.`) using the `Dockerfile` and runs the command `npm start`. Its container is named **myapp_web_1**, appears on the network\u202f`front-tier` as **myapp_web**, and is assigned the hostname **webhost** with the domain name **example.com**. It uses the `node:14\u2011alpine` image, sets the entrypoint to `/docker\u2011entrypoint.sh`, and launches under the `node` user. Resource limits include 512\u202fcpu shares, a CPU set of `0,1`, a memory limit of\u202f`512m` with a swap limit of\u202f`1g`, and a MAC address of `02:42:ac:11:00:02`. The container is granted access to the sound device (`/dev/snd`), mounts the current directory into `/usr/src/app` and a `logs` volume into `/var/log/app`, uses the local volume driver, and also inherits the `data_volume` via `volumes_from`. DNS is configured with `8.8.8.8` and `8.8.4.4`, a DNS search domain of `example.com`, and an extra host entry mapping `host.docker.internal` to `host-gateway`. It exposes port\u202f3000 internally, publishes ports `80:80` and `443:443` externally, and links to the **db** service as well as an external link `redis:redis`. Logging is handled by the `json\u2011file` driver with a maximum size of `10m`. The container runs in a host IPC namespace, has no PID namespace set, and is not privileged or read\u2011only. It starts with an interactive TTY and keeps stdin open, restarts always, and applies the security option `no-new-privileges`. Labels identify it as a \u201cWeb service\u201d (`com.example.description=Web service`). Environment variables are drawn from the `.env` file and explicitly set to `NODE_ENV=production`, `PORT=3000`, and `DEBUG=false`.\n\nThe **db** service uses the `postgres:13` image and is named **myapp_db_1**. Its environment is supplied as a list with `POSTGRES_PASSWORD=example` and `POSTGRES_DB=mydb`. It publishes the database port `5432:5432`, stores data in the `db_data` volume mounted at `/var/lib/postgresql/data`, and restarts on failure. A label marks its role as a database (`com.example.role=db`)."
